# Copy this file to .env and change what you need.
# Each line is commented out and shows the default value. Remove the "#" to change a value.
# A switch takes 1 or 0. It also takes true or false, yes or no, and on or off. An empty value means 0.
# When the server cannot use a value, it stops at start, and the log names the variable.
# The README has the same list as a table, with the measured numbers.

# ---- Ports ----

# Port of the OpenAI-compatible API on the host. The container keeps port 8000.
# Change it when another program uses port 8000 on the host.
# To turn the API off with docker-compose.yml, remove its line from "ports". Without Docker Compose, 0 turns it off.
# HTTP_PORT=8000

# Port of the Wyoming server for Home Assistant on the host. The container keeps port 10200.
# Change it when another program uses port 10200 on the host.
# To turn the server off with docker-compose.yml, remove its line from "ports". Without Docker Compose, 0 turns it off.
# WYOMING_PORT=10200

# Network address that the API and the Wyoming server listen on. 0.0.0.0 means all addresses.
# In a container, keep it. Without Docker, set 127.0.0.1 to accept only requests from the same computer.
# HTTP_HOST=0.0.0.0
# WYOMING_HOST=0.0.0.0

# ---- Voice and speed ----

# Voice for requests without a voice, and for unknown voice names.
# It must be a name from GET /v1/audio/voices.
# Change it to use another voice in the Wyoming integration, or with clients that send a name such as "alloy".
# DEFAULT_VOICE=Speaker_43

# Speed of the Wyoming speech, and of OpenAI requests without a speed. The range is 0.5 to 2.0.
# A value outside the range stops the server.
# Change it when the speech is too fast or too slow. The Wyoming protocol has no speed field.
# DEFAULT_SPEED=1.0

# 1 writes numbers, dates, units and acronyms as words before the speech (verbalizer). 0 turns the verbalizer off.
# AUTO_USE_VERBALIZER is the old name. The server reads it when VERBALIZE is not set.
# Set 0 only when your texts have no digits or symbols.
# Then the server does not download the verbalizer (1.9 GB) and saves about 0.5 GB of memory.
# VERBALIZE=1

# ---- Models and memory ----

# Where the speech model runs: cpu or cuda. The CPU image sets cpu. The CUDA image sets cuda.
# Leave it. Choose the image tag that fits your hardware. The CPU image cannot use cuda.
# DEVICE=cpu

# Where the verbalizer runs: cpu or cuda. The default is the value of DEVICE.
# In the CUDA image, set cpu to keep the verbalizer off the GPU, for example when the GPU has little free memory.
# VERBALIZER_DEVICE=cpu

# 1: at start, the server loads the models one at a time in the background.
# A request during this load does not wait for the end of the load. It loads the models that its text needs.
# 0: the models load at the first request. The model process and the voice list still start with the server.
# Keep 1, so the first request is fast and the downloads of the first start finish early.
# PRELOAD=1

# Seconds without requests, after which the server unloads the models. 0 never unloads.
# The model process stays with its libraries, about 0.44 GB.
# The next request takes about 3.5 s instead of about 1.3 s.
# Set it, for example to 600, when the host needs the memory for other work.
# UNLOAD_AFTER_SECONDS=0

# Seconds without use, after which the server unloads only the verbalizer. 0 keeps it loaded once it is loaded.
# When the value is above 0, PRELOAD and the warm-up skip the verbalizer.
# It loads for a text with digits, symbols, Latin letters or acronyms. This request takes 0.4 to 0.6 s more.
# Set it to give back about 0.5 GB when most of your texts have no digits or symbols.
# Use a value below UNLOAD_AFTER_SECONDS.
# VERBALIZER_UNLOAD_AFTER_SECONDS=0

# ---- CPU ----

# CPU threads for each model.
# 0 uses the CPU limit of the container, rounded up. For example, --cpus 4 gives 4 threads.
# Without a limit, 0 uses all cores. The server reads the limit on hosts with cgroup v2.
# Set it when the host runs other heavy work, or when you want the server to use fewer cores.
# THREADS=0

# ---- Paths and downloads ----

# Folder in the container for your voices (voices) and the cache (cache). The Dockerfile sets it.
# Do not change it. Mount your host folder to /data.
# DATA_DIR=/data

# Folder for the downloaded models. The download library reads it. The Dockerfile sets it.
# Do not change it.
# HF_HOME=/data/huggingface

# Folder for the stress model. The stress library reads it. The Dockerfile sets it.
# Do not change it.
# STANZA_RESOURCES_DIR=/data/stanza

# Hugging Face access token. The download library reads it.
# Set it when Hugging Face limits the downloads of the first start.
# HF_TOKEN=

# User and group of the container. Only docker-compose.yml reads them.
# Change them when the folder ./data belongs to another user. Make sure that this user can write into it.
# PUID=1000
# PGID=1000

# ---- Logs ----

# Amount of log text: DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, ERROR or CRITICAL.
# INFO logs the text of each request. DEBUG also logs the verbalized text and the phonemes.
# Set DEBUG to find out why a word sounds wrong. Set WARNING to keep the request texts out of the log.
# LOG_LEVEL=INFO
